diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..9161453 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,39 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Sign-up phone verification
+
+The sign-up form requests an SMS code through `POST /api/signup` (under the configured
+Astro base path). The server uses Twilio Verify and only calls the existing registration
+API after Twilio approves the phone/code pair. Codes and provider credentials are never
+returned to the client. The existing external registration API is independently hosted;
+requiring verification for all callers of that API also requires enforcement there.
+
+Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, and `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID` as runtime
+environment variables on the Node server (see `.env.example`). Without them the endpoint
+returns an unavailable message; it does not simulate SMS delivery. Configure the Verify
+service for **six-digit codes**, enable Fraud Guard, and configure provider-side rate
+limits and destination permissions. The form also applies a 30-second resend cooldown;
+provider-side limits enforce protection independently of the browser.
+
+For automatic code extraction, configure an approved Twilio Verify custom SMS template
+as the service default. It must end with the website hostname and the generated code:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 123456.
+
+@your-deployed-hostname.example #123456
+```
+
+Use the template's dynamic code placeholder in place of the example code. The hostname
+must match the page receiving the SMS, without a scheme, port, or path. See
+[Twilio verification templates](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates)
+and [Chrome's WebOTP guidance](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp).
+WebOTP requires HTTPS and browser permission. Safari can suggest codes via
+`autocomplete="one-time-code"`; manual entry and paste remain available everywhere.
+The form starts listening before requesting delivery and aborts on submission, resend,
+changing details, timeout, or unmount. A filled code still requires the user to submit.
+
+Run server-side verification tests with `node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/signup.test.mjs`.
+Tests mock all provider and registration requests and do not send SMS or create accounts.
